From 5ca2a999bf7302136935eae8f85a932121adc4f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 23:29:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07257/11362] [outer-loop] lf52 live-parity fix: in-bounds
 L9-L10 route, LIVE-validated to L10

lf52 was solved offline 10/10 but its banked L9-L10 tail clicked 22 out-of-bounds
ACTION6 coordinates (x up to 132 / down to -8; valid range 0-63) addressing
off-screen blue relay pegs (source grid x~11-21). The offline arcade routes those
permissively; the live API rejects them with HTTP 400 at action 849, capping live
depth at L8.

Root cause: the original route walked the east blue relays westward while the
camera was still at the level-start offset and no green was loaded on the carrier,
so those pegs were off-screen. L9 camera model: render pixel = 6*grid + offset;
scripted -20px pan on any peg landing at (6,5); -6px carrier-follow pan per
green-loaded ACTION1-4 move (empty/blue carrier does not pan); carrier rail is
row 5, x=6-20.

Fix (development_proxy, restructures only the L9 completion; L1-L8 prefix and
fresh-init L10 suffix unchanged): use the carried green as a camera crane so every
ACTION6 target renders within 0-63, found by constrained best-first search over a
faithful pure-Python L9 model cross-checked op-by-op against the real engine.

Validation: 0 OOB clicks; fresh offline replay -> GameState.WIN (L10);
reproduce(claimed_level=10) reproduced=True; 5/5 fresh replays; and LIVE VALIDATE
(scorecard opened, NOT closed; no --submit) reached live L10 with all 1033 actions
accepted past the original action-849 failure. lf52 live-submittable depth: L8 -> L10.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
